{"id":"prepositions-0061","taskId":"prepositions","title":"Drill set 61","text":null,"source":"drill","gaps":[{"answer":"to","accept":[],"options":[],"base":null,"keyword":null,"lead":null,"sentence":"Her style is similar ___ her sister\u0027s.","hint":"similar ___ sth","explanation":"similar TO something (never \u0027than\u0027)."},{"answer":"with","accept":[],"options":[],"base":null,"keyword":null,"lead":null,"sentence":"We\u0027re not entirely satisfied ___ the service.","hint":"satisfied ___ sth","explanation":"satisfied WITH something."},{"answer":"to","accept":[],"options":[],"base":null,"keyword":null,"lead":null,"sentence":"Be kind ___ your little brother.","hint":"kind ___ sb","explanation":"kind TO somebody."},{"answer":"for","accept":[],"options":[],"base":null,"keyword":null,"lead":null,"sentence":"We\u0027re hoping ___ the best results this season.","hint":"hope ___ sth (want)","explanation":"hope FOR something = want and expect it."},{"answer":"to","accept":["towards"],"options":[],"base":null,"keyword":null,"lead":null,"sentence":"His attitude ___ work has really improved.","hint":"attitude ___ sth","explanation":"attitude TO (or TOWARDS) something."},{"answer":"at","accept":[],"options":[],"base":null,"keyword":null,"lead":null,"sentence":"Please don\u0027t shout ___ the children.","hint":"shout ___ sb (angrily)","explanation":"shout AT somebody = be aggressive; shout TO = call so they hear."},{"answer":"from","accept":[],"options":[],"base":null,"keyword":null,"lead":null,"sentence":"The results differ sharply ___ last year\u0027s.","hint":"differ ___ sth","explanation":"differ FROM something (one thing differs from another); differ WITH = disagree."},{"answer":"to","accept":[],"options":[],"base":null,"keyword":null,"lead":null,"sentence":"Staff must always be polite ___ customers.","hint":"polite ___ sb","explanation":"polite TO somebody."}]}